{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01At2H5KJqQZHHzMBt5SCWbB","type":"tool_result","content":"    assert set(sw.CUT_LEMMA_PROVED) <= set(sw.ALL_PROVED)\n    code = re.sub(r\"/-.*?-/\", \"\", src, flags=re.S)\n    code = re.sub(r\"--.*\", \"\", code)\n    assert \"sorry\" not in code\n    assert not re.search(r\"^\\s*axiom\\b\", code, re.M)\n    root = (CUT_LEMMA_LEAN.parents[2] / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    assert \"import MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.CutLemma\\n\" in root\n    axioms = (CUT_LEMMA_LEAN.parents[3] / \"paper1\" / \"axiom_check.lean\").read_text()\n    for n in sw.CUT_LEMMA_PROVED:\n        assert f\"#print axioms MOSPFormalization.{n}\\n\" in axioms, n\n    for n in (\"pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary\", \"pathwidth_le_cut\",\n              \"pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree\", \"pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul\"):\n        assert n in sw.CUT_LEMMA_PROVED\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# item 05: `lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/Potential.lean`\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nPOTENTIAL_LEAN = WEIGHTS_LEAN.parent / \"Potential.lean\"\n\n\ndef test_potential_minus_lean_transcription_agrees_with_fminus():\n    \"\"\"The Lean `potentialMinus` (transcribed) equals the Python `fminus` and its per-vertex\n    form on random graphs with isolated vertices; additivity holds on disjoint unions.\"\"\"\n    import random\n    import learning.sandwich as sw\n    from learning.edwards_mcdermid import fminus, support\n    rng = random.Random(505)\n    for _ in range(200):\n        n = rng.randint(1, 11)\n        adj = sw._random_graph_with_isolated(rng, n)\n        assert sw.potential_minus_lean(adj) == fminus(adj)\n        assert sw.potential_minus_lean(adj) == sw.vertex_term_sum_lean(adj)\n        # a disjoint union with a second random graph on the complementary vertices\n        s = support(adj)\n        rest = [v for v in range(n) if not (s >> v) & 1]\n        g2 = [0] * n\n        for i, u in enumerate(rest):\n            for v in rest[i + 1:]:\n                if rng.random() < 0.6:\n                    g2[u] |= 1 << v\n                    g2[v] |= 1 << u\n        union = [a | b for a, b in zip(adj, g2)]\n        assert sw.potential_minus_lean(union) == sw.potential_minus_lean(adj) + sw.potential_minus_lean(g2)\n\n\ndef test_potential_proved_names_are_theorems_in_the_lean_file():\n    \"\"\"Every name `learning.sandwich` audits for `Potential.lean` is declared there as a\n    theorem; the file has no `sorry` and no `axiom`; the root module imports it; and\n    `paper1/axiom_check.lean` prints the axioms of every one.\"\"\"\n    import learning.sandwich as sw\n    src = POTENTIAL_LEAN.read_text()\n    declared = set(re.findall(r\"^(?:@\\[simp\\] )?theorem\\s+([^\\s:({\\[]+)\", src, re.M))\n    missing = [n for n in sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED if n.split(\".\")[-1] not in declared]\n    assert not missing, missing\n    assert all(n.startswith(\"DegreeBound.\") for n in sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED)\n    assert set(sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED) <= set(sw.ALL_PROVED)\n    assert len(sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED) == len(declared) == 54\n    code = re.sub(r\"/-.*?-/\", \"\", src, flags=re.S)\n    code = re.sub(r\"--.*\", \"\", code)\n    assert \"sorry\" not in code\n    assert not re.search(r\"^\\s*axiom\\b\", code, re.M)\n    root = (POTENTIAL_LEAN.parents[2] / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    assert \"import MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.Potential\\n\" in root\n    axioms = (POTENTIAL_LEAN.parents[3] / \"paper1\" / \"axiom_check.lean\").read_text()\n    for n in sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED:\n        assert f\"#print axioms MOSPFormalization.{n}\\n\" in axioms, n\n    for n in (\"degree_isolate\", \"potential_isolate\", \"potential_isolate_le_sub_one\",\n              \"potential_isolate_regular\", \"potentialMinus_le_potential\",\n              \"potentialMinus_eq_sum_compPotential\", \"compPotential_nonneg\",\n              \"potentialMinus_eq_sum_vertexTerm\", \"potentialMinus_le_F\",\n              \"potentialMinus_eq_F_of_connected\", \"potentialMinus_add\",\n              \"potentialMinus_cubic\", \"potentialMinus_ge_five_sixths\"):\n        assert f\"DegreeBound.{n}\" in sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# item 06: `lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/SPReduction.lean` — the reduction system\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSP_REDUCTION_LEAN = WEIGHTS_LEAN.parent / \"SPReduction.lean\"\n\n\ndef _step_kind(adj, v):\n    nb = adj[v]\n    if nb.bit_count() == 1:\n        return \"pendant\"\n    x = (nb & -nb).bit_length() - 1\n    y = (nb ^ (nb & -nb)).bit_length() - 1\n    return \"triangle\" if (adj[x] >> y) & 1 else \"suppress\"\n\n\ndef test_commutation_lemma_in_the_lean_form_on_random_graphs():\n    \"\"\"R3 as `SPStep.isolate_comm` proves it: for a step at `v` and `w ≠ v`, either\n    `H − w = G − w` (then `v` was pendant at `w`) or one step at `v` in `G − w` reaches\n    `H − w`, pendant if `w ∈ N(v)` and of the original kind otherwise; R3X for a random\n    finset `X ∌ v`; R4 along a random maximal reduction with `X ⊆ supp H`; R5 with a\n    graph `K` supported away from `G`; a vertex of degree 1 or 2 admits a step (the\n    witness of `exists_spStep_of_ndeg`).\"\"\"\n    import random\n    from learning.edwards_mcdermid import (bits, isolate, isolate_set, sp_step, step_vertices,\n                                          support)\n    rng = random.Random(606)\n    triples = 0\n    for _ in range(300):\n        n = rng.randint(2, 11)\n        p = rng.choice([0.15, 0.3, 0.5])\n        adj = [0] * n\n        for a in range(n):\n            for b in range(a + 1, n):\n                if rng.random() < p:\n                    adj[a] |= 1 << b\n                    adj[b] |= 1 << a\n        for v in step_vertices(adj):\n            H = sp_step(adj, v)\n            kind = _step_kind(adj, v)\n            assert H[v] == 0 and sum(h.bit_count() for h in H) < sum(a.bit_count() for a in adj)\n            assert all(H[u].bit_count() <= adj[u].bit_count() for u in range(n))\n            for w in range(n):\n                if w == v:\n                    continue\n                triples += 1\n                Gw, Hw = isolate(adj, w), isolate(H, w)\n                if Hw == Gw:\n                    assert kind == \"pendant\" and (adj[v] >> w) & 1\n                    continue\n                assert 1 <= Gw[v].bit_count() <= 2 and sp_step(Gw, v) == Hw\n                assert _step_kind(Gw, v) == (\"pendant\" if (adj[v] >> w) & 1 else kind)\n            X = sum(1 << u for u in range(n) if u != v and rng.random() < 0.4)\n            GX, HX = isolate_set(adj, X), isolate_set(H, X)\n            assert HX == GX or (1 <= GX[v].bit_count() <= 2 and sp_step(GX, v) == HX)\n            s = support(adj)\n            rest = [u for u in range(n) if not (s >> u) & 1]\n            K = [0] * n\n            for i, a in enumerate(rest):\n                for b in rest[i + 1:]:\n                    if rng.random() < 0.6:\n                        K[a] |= 1 << b\n                        K[b] |= 1 << a\n            GK = [a | k for a, k in zip(adj, K)]\n            assert sp_step(GK, v) == [h | k for h, k in zip(H, K)]\n        # R4 along a random maximal reduction\n        seq, cur = [], list(adj)\n        while step_vertices(cur):\n            v = rng.choice(step_vertices(cur))\n            seq.append(v)\n            cur = sp_step(cur, v)\n        assert all(cur[v] == 0 for v in seq)\n        X = sum(1 << u for u in bits(support(cur)) if rng.random() < 0.5)\n        g_cur = isolate_set(adj, X)\n        for v in seq:\n            assert not (X >> v) & 1\n            if 1 <= g_cur[v].bit_count() <= 2:\n                g_cur = sp_step(g_cur, v)\n        assert g_cur == isolate_set(cur, X)\n    assert triples > 1000\n\n\ndef test_item06_brute_force_log_has_no_violation():\n    \"\"\"The exhaustive check to 9 vertices (`06_reduction/check_r3.py`) was run and found\n    nothing; its R3 counts are item 02's.\"\"\"\n    import json\n    p = SP_REDUCTION_LEAN.parents[3] / \"reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/06_reduction/summary.json\"\n    if not p.exists():\n        pytest.skip(\"brute-force summary not present\")\n    s = json.loads(p.read_text())\n    assert s[\"violations\"] == 0\n    assert s[\"total\"][\"R3\"] == 3115987 and s[\"total\"][\"R3_zero\"] == 95300\n    assert s[\"total\"][\"R1\"] == 393156\n\n\ndef test_sp_reduction_proved_names_are_theorems_in_the_lean_file():\n    \"\"\"Every name `learning.sandwich` audits for `SPReduction.lean` is declared there as a\n    theorem (namespaces resolved); the file has no `sorry` and no `axiom`; the root module\n    imports it; `paper1/axiom_check.lean` prints the axioms of every one; the statements\n    the later items need are present.\"\"\"\n    import learning.sandwich as sw\n    src = SP_REDUCTION_LEAN.read_text()\n    code = re.sub(r\"/-.*?-/\", \"\", src, flags=re.S)\n    ns, declared = [], set()\n----SW\nSP_REDUCTION_PROVED = (\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_eq_degree\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_eq_zero_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_pos_of_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_le_of_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_bot\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_eq_one_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_eq_two_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_sup\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_edge_left\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_edge_right\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_edge_of_ne\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_eq_self_of_forall_not_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_eq_self_of_ndeg_eq_zero\",\n    \"DegreeBound.neighborSet_isolate\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_isolate_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_isolate_self\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_empty\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_singleton\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_insert\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_comm_isolate\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_isolateSet_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_eq_self\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_sup_restrict_compl\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_restrict\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_adj_imp_not_adj_compl\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isSPReduced_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isSPReduced_bot\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isBasic_bot\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.refl\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.trans\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.single\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.head\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.tail\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.not_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_self\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.exists_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_pos\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_eq\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_isolate_sup_edge_left\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_isolate_sup_edge_of_ne\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.degSum_lt\",\n    \"DegreeBound.not_isSPReduced_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.exists_spStep_of_ndeg\",\n    \"DegreeBound.exists_spStep_of_not_isSPReduced\",\n    \"DegreeBound.IsSPReduced.not_spStep\",\n    \"DegreeBound.exists_reduced_reduct\",\n    \"DegreeBound.IsSPReduced.eq_of_spReduces\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.ndeg_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.degree_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.ndeg_eq_zero\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.not_adj_of_not_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.supp_subset\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.potential_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.potential_sub_ge_of_isolated\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.isolate_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.isolateSet_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.sup_of_disjoint\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.not_spStep_of_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.isolateSet_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.isolate_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.isolate_comm_of_isolated\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.sup_of_disjoint\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.sup_of_disjoint_supp\",\n)\n#: Every proved name the axiom check asks for.\nALL_PROVED = (PROVED + FOREST_COVER_PROVED + PENDANT_PROVED + SEPARATOR_PROVED + DEGREE_BOUND_PROVED\n              + CUT_LEMMA_PROVED + POTENTIAL_PROVED + SP_REDUCTION_PROVED)\n#: Statements committed with `sorry`: none since 2026-10-31.\nSTATED: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# The Lean definitions, transcribed\n----GATE\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Regression gate for loop0012 (the Edwards–McDermid degree-sequence bound).\n\nPasses only if all five hold:\n1. `lake build` in lean/ succeeds;\n2. every `.lean` file under lean/MOSPFormalization/ (top level, Complex/ and\n   Search/) is imported by lean/MOSPFormalization.lean, so the build really\n   checks it;\n3. the number of `sorry` in Lean *code* (comments and docstrings stripped) is\n   at most the baseline (0: the development has none since Appendix E) plus\n   the entries in allowed_sorries.txt, and no `axiom` declaration exists;\n4. `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes, and so does `pytest` in\n   pathwidth_solver/;\n5. the paper builds with no undefined references (`make -C paper1/latex check`).\n\n    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0012/gate.py\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[1]\nLEAN = REPO / \"lean\"\nBASELINE_SORRIES = 0\nALLOWED = HERE / \"allowed_sorries.txt\"\nPAPER = REPO / \"paper1\" / \"latex\"\n\n\ndef strip_comments(src: str) -> str:\n    out, i, depth = [], 0, 0\n    while i < len(src):\n        if src.startswith(\"/-\", i):\n            depth += 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth and src.startswith(\"-/\", i):\n            depth -= 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth:\n            i += 1; continue\n        if src.startswith(\"--\", i):\n            j = src.find(\"\\n\", i); i = len(src) if j < 0 else j; continue\n        if src[i] == '\"':\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(src) and src[j] != '\"':\n                j += 2 if src[j] == \"\\\\\" else 1\n            i = j + 1; continue\n        out.append(src[i]); i += 1\n    return \"\".join(out)\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    ok = True\n    b = subprocess.run([\"lake\", \"build\"], cwd=LEAN, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    tail = \"\\n\".join((b.stdout + b.stderr).splitlines()[-25:])\n    if b.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: lake build\\n\" + tail); return 1\n    print(\"lake build: ok\")\n\n    root = (LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        mod = \"MOSPFormalization.\" + \".\".join(f.relative_to(LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").with_suffix(\"\").parts)\n        if not re.search(rf\"^import {re.escape(mod)}\\s*$\", root, re.M):\n            print(f\"GATE FAIL: {mod} is not imported by MOSPFormalization.lean\"); ok = False\n\n    sorries, axioms = [], []\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        code = strip_comments(f.read_text())\n        for n, line in enumerate(code.splitlines(), 1):\n            if re.search(r\"\\bsorry\\b\", line):\n                sorries.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n            if re.match(r\"\\s*(private\\s+)?axiom\\b\", line):\n                axioms.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n    allowed = [l for l in ALLOWED.read_text().splitlines() if l.strip() and not l.startswith(\"#\")] if ALLOWED.exists() else []\n    limit = BASELINE_SORRIES + len(allowed)\n    print(f\"sorry in code: {len(sorries)} (limit {limit}): {sorries}\")\n    if len(sorries) > limit:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: more sorry than the baseline plus allowed_sorries.txt\"); ok = False\n    if axioms:\n----MINOR\n154:def isolate (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : SimpleGraph V where\n155-  Adj x y := G.Adj x y ∧ x ≠ v ∧ y ≠ v\n156-  symm := ⟨fun _ _ ⟨h, hx, hy⟩ => ⟨h.symm, hy, hx⟩⟩\n157-  loopless := ⟨fun x h => G.loopless.irrefl x h.1⟩\n158-\n159-theorem isolate_le (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : isolate G v ≤ G := fun _ _ h => h.1\n160-\n----REPORT6\n## 6. Lean (iii): the series-parallel reduction system, basic graphs, degree monotonicity, and the commutation of deletion with reduction (item 06, 2026-11-02)\n\n**Deliverable.** `lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/SPReduction.lean`\n(namespace `MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound`, imports `Potential`): the four\noperations of Edwards & McDermid (2015, p. 8) as a step relation on\n`SimpleGraph V` with removed vertices isolated, its reflexive–transitive\nclosure, \"reduced\", \"basic\", and **69 theorems, no `sorry`, no `axiom`**,\nevery one `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. R1–R5 of §2.2 are all\nproved; R6 (optional, not needed by the assembly) is not. No confluence fact\nis stated or used: the paper's Lemma 3.1 (which cites Kneis et al. 2009) is\nreplaced by the local commutation lemma R3 and its lifts R3X / R4, as plan\n§0.5 said. Imported by `lean/MOSPFormalization.lean`; `lake build` passes\n(`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/06_reduction/lake_build.log`).\n\n**Regenerate.** `cd lean && lake build`; `make -C paper1/latex axioms`;\n`nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/06_reduction/check_r3.py --max-n 9 --workers 8`\n(3 s on 8 workers at load 0.3; `check_r3.log`, `summary.json`).\n\n**Size range.** The Lean statements hold on every finite graph (kernel-checked).\nThe brute-force check is every graph on 1–9 vertices from `nauty-geng`\n(288,266), exhaustive for R1, R2, R3, EX, and random for the finset and\nsequence forms (R3X, R4, R5); nothing beyond 9 vertices was checked.\n\n### 6.1 Checked before stated (`06_reduction/check_r3.py`, `check_r3.log`, `summary.json`)\n\nItem 02 had R1–R5 on every graph to 9 (§2.3); the item asked for R3's stage\nto be re-run here. It was re-run **in the form the Lean proof produces**, which\nis stronger than item 02's: R3 records not only that `H − w = G − w` or that\none step at `v` in `G − w` reaches `H − w`, but *which* case and *which\nconstructor* — zero steps exactly when `v` is pendant at `w`; one step of the\noriginal kind when `w ∉ N(v)`, a pendant deletion when `w ∈ N(v)`. The\nstatements beyond §2.6 (R3X, the hypothesis form of R4, R5 in the `⊔` form,\nthe step-existence lemma) were checked for the first time.\n\n| statement | checked on | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| EX: a vertex of degree 1 or 2 admits a step (`exists_spStep_of_ndeg`) | 2,579,255 (graph, vertex) | 0 failures |\n| R1: `degSum H < degSum G` and `ndeg H v = 0 < ndeg G v` | 393,156 steps | 0 |\n| R2: no degree rises; `f H ≤ f G`; an isolated vertex costs `≥ g(deg)` | 393,156 steps, every vertex | 0 |\n| R3 with the constructor kind | 3,115,987 (graph, step, `w`): **95,300 zero-step, all pendant-at-`w`; 3,020,687 one-step, all of the predicted kind** | 0 |\n| R3X: `v ∉ X` random (3 per step) | 1,179,468 (257,776 zero, 921,692 one) | 0 |\n| R4: replay along a random maximal reduction with random `X ⊆ supp H` | 864,798 (graph, `X`) over 288,266 sequences; every acted vertex isolated in `H` | 0 |\n| R5: `SPStep (G ⊔ K) v (H ⊔ K)`, same kind, `K` random on `V ∖ supp G` | 25,566 | 0 |\n\nThe R3 totals (3,115,987 / 95,300 / 3,020,687) are item 02's to the triple.\n**Kill checks: none fired.**\n\n### 6.2 Definitions\n\n- `ndeg G v := (G.neighborSet v).ncard` — the degree with no decidability\n  instance; `ndeg_eq_degree` pins it to `G.degree v` under any\n  `DecidableRel G.Adj`; `degSum G := ∑ v, ndeg G v`.\n- `isolateSet G X` (`G − X`, `X : Finset V`): `Adj a b := G.Adj a b ∧ a ∉ X ∧ b ∉ X`;\n  `restrict G S` (`G|S`, `S : Set V`): `Adj a b := G.Adj a b ∧ a ∈ S ∧ b ∈ S`.\n- `inductive SPStep (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : SimpleGraph V → Prop` with\n  `pendant (hx : G.Adj v x) (hall : ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x) : SPStep G v (isolate G v)`\n  (operation 2), `suppress (hx) (hy) (hxy : x ≠ y) (hall : ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x ∨ z = y) (hnadj : ¬ G.Adj x y) : SPStep G v (isolate G v ⊔ edge x y)`\n  (operation 3), `triangle (…) (hadj : G.Adj x y) : SPStep G v (isolate G v)`\n  (operation 4). Operation 1 is the identity on `SimpleGraph V` (§2.1 (1)).\n- `SPReduces G H := Relation.ReflTransGen (fun G H => ∃ v, SPStep G v H) G H`;\n  `IsSPReduced G := ∀ v, ndeg G v = 0 ∨ 3 ≤ ndeg G v`;\n  `IsBasic G := ∀ C : G.ConnectedComponent, (∃ v ∈ C.supp, 0 < ndeg G v) → (∀ v ∈ C.supp, ndeg G v = 3) ∨ ∃ v ∈ C.supp, SPReduces (isolate (restrict G C.supp) v) ⊥`.\n\n### 6.3 The statements and their proofs\n\nThe instance-free degree (7): `ndeg_eq_degree`, `ndeg_eq_zero_iff`\n(`↔ ∀ z, ¬ G.Adj v z`), `ndeg_pos_of_adj`, `ndeg_le_of_le`, `ndeg_bot`,\n`ndeg_eq_one_iff` (`↔ ∃ x, G.Adj v x ∧ ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x`, from\n....\n### 6.4 Choices beyond §2.6\n\n1. **The step carries its vertex and states the neighbourhood by adjacency\n   facts, not degrees.** `SPStep G v H` (the item's \"if R3's acted-on vertex\n   needs to be recorded, make `SPStep` carry it from the start\": it does —\n   R3 is stated at `v`, and R4's induction needs `v ∉ X`). The constructors\n   take `G.Adj v x` and `∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x` (or `z = x ∨ z = y` with\n   `x ≠ y`) rather than `G.degree v = 1` / `2`, so the relation needs no\n   decidability instance and the case analysis of R3 is propositional\n   (`tauto` closes every graph identity).\n2. **An instance-free degree.** `exists_reduced_reduct`'s `H` and the\n   intermediate graphs of every `ReflTransGen` induction carry no\n   `DecidableRel`; `ndeg` (`Set.ncard`) makes `IsSPReduced`, `IsBasic`, R1 and\n   R2 instance-free, and `ndeg_eq_degree` (any instance) converts at the\n   boundary. No `Subsingleton.elim` on instances was needed anywhere.\n3. **R1 on the degree sum, not the edge count.** §2.6 listed\n   `SPStep.edgeFinset_card_lt`; the degree sum drops by 2 (pendant,\n   suppression) or 4 (triangle), and its strict decrease is R2 plus the\n   strict drop at `v` — one `Finset.sum_lt_sum` instead of an edge-set case\n   analysis. `degSum` is the measure of the strong induction.\n4. **`isolateSet` is defined directly**, not as the fold of `isolate` (plan\n   §0.5); `isolateSet_insert` is the fold's step and `isolateSet_singleton`\n   the base, so the fold is recoverable as a theorem.\n5. **R4's hypothesis is `∀ w ∈ X, ∃ z, H.Adj w z`** (`X ⊆ supp H`), the\n   parenthetical option of §2.6, and the proof is by head induction on the\n   sequence rather than by induction on `X` first: an acted vertex ends\n   isolated and stays isolated, so `X ⊆ supp H` keeps `X` clear of every step,\n   and R3X (proved by `Finset` induction from R3) does one step at a time. A\n   Finset-first induction would need the hypothesis for `X ∖ {w}` on\n   `H − w`, where `w`'s removal can isolate other vertices of `X` — the form\n   §2.6 wrote does not go through directly; this one does, and it is the\n   form item 08 uses (`X* ⊆ supp G*`).\n6. **R5's disjointness is instance-free**, `∀ a b, K.Adj a b → ∀ z, ¬ G.Adj a z`,\n   with the `supp` form as a corollary; along a sequence it is preserved\n   because supports shrink.\n7. **`restrict` lives here** (item 05 left it to item 08), with\n   `restrict_sup_restrict_compl`, `isolate_restrict` and `restrict_eq_self`\n   for item 08's disconnected case and for item 07's `nonbasic_reduct_ne_bot`\n   (where the support is one component and `restrict G C.supp = G`).\n8. **R6 is not proved.** It is optional, not what A1 needs, and the budget\n   went to R3–R5.\n\n### 6.5 Axiom lines, tests, regenerate\n\n- 69 new `#print axioms` lines in `paper1/axiom_check.lean`\n  (`06_reduction/axiom_check.log`); `make -C paper1/latex axioms`: **494\n  theorems checked, 0 failures**, every line `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.\n  `SP_REDUCTION_PROVED` (69 names) is folded into `learning.sandwich.ALL_PROVED`.\n- Tests: 3 new in `tests/test_edwards_mcdermid.py` (41 in all): R3 in the\n  Lean form (constructor kinds), R3X, R4 along random maximal reductions, R5\n  and EX on 300 random graphs at 2–11 vertices; the brute-force summary's\n  counts and zero violations; the 69 names declared (namespaces resolved) /\n  imported / audited, no `sorry`, no `axiom`, the constructors and\n  definitions present.\n- No new sandwich stage: nothing here is numerical. The item's\n  `potential_le` and `potential_sub_ge_of_isolated` are the Lean forms of the\n  R2 rows item 02 checked (`R2f`, `R2iso`).\n\n### 6.6 Kill verdict, and what this does not claim\n\n**Kill verdict: none** (the item has no kill criterion); R3 and R4 fitted, so\nitem 08 states Theorem 3.2 with `SPReduces (G − X) B` as the plan wrote it,\nnot with the paper's `r(G − X) = B` and a `ReductionConfluence` Prop.\n\n**What items 07–09 get.** `SPStep`, `SPReduces`, `IsSPReduced`, `IsBasic`,\n`ndeg`, `isolateSet`, `restrict`; `exists_reduced_reduct` (the `G*` of the\nstep); `SPReduces.ndeg_le` / `degree_le` / `potential_le` /\n`potential_sub_ge_of_isolated` (the hinge `j₄ ≥ g'(d)` of item 07: a vertex\nof degree `d ≥ 3` in `G − w` either survives into `G*` with degree `≤ d`, so\n`g'(δ(G*)) ≥ g'(d)` by W3, or is isolated, so `f(G − w) − f(G*) ≥ g(d) ≥ g'(d)`);\n`IsSPReduced.eq_of_spReduces` and `isSPReduced_iff`; R4\n`SPReduces.isolateSet_comm` with `X* ⊆ supp G*` (item 08's\n`SPReduces (G − w − X*) (G* − X*)`); R5 `SPReduces.sup_of_disjoint` with\n`restrict_sup_restrict_compl` and `potentialMinus_add` (item 08's\ndisconnected case); `IsBasic`'s second clause is existential over reduction\nsequences, so `nonbasic_reduct_ne_bot` (item 07) needs no confluence.\n\n**Does not claim.** Uniqueness of the reduct (measured to 9 in item 02, not\nneeded, not proved); that `SPReduces G ⊥` characterises series-parallel\ngraphs (the paper's \"it follows from the definition\" is not formalised and\n\"series-parallel\" does not appear in Lean); R6; anything about pathwidth\n(item 09) or about the hypotheses (H1), (H3); that the brute-force counts are\nevidence beyond 9 vertices (the Lean theorems are the evidence for every\nfinite graph). The constructor-kind refinement of R3 is a property of *this*\nproof's case analysis, recorded so a reader can match the check to the\nproof, not a claim that the kind is forced.\n/usr/bin/nauty-geng\n01_verify\n02_lemmas\n03_weights\n04_cut\n05_potential\n06_reduction\nSHA256\nem2015.pdf\nem2015.txt","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0876bac-7461-4cfb-84fd-1d355ecb73ab","uuid":"cf963500-4946-4720-9f8c-84f00db45194","timestamp":"2026-11-02T04:11:09.219Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"    assert set(sw.CUT_LEMMA_PROVED) <= set(sw.ALL_PROVED)\n    code = re.sub(r\"/-.*?-/\", \"\", src, flags=re.S)\n    code = re.sub(r\"--.*\", \"\", code)\n    assert \"sorry\" not in code\n    assert not re.search(r\"^\\s*axiom\\b\", code, re.M)\n    root = (CUT_LEMMA_LEAN.parents[2] / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    assert \"import MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.CutLemma\\n\" in root\n    axioms = (CUT_LEMMA_LEAN.parents[3] / \"paper1\" / \"axiom_check.lean\").read_text()\n    for n in sw.CUT_LEMMA_PROVED:\n        assert f\"#print axioms MOSPFormalization.{n}\\n\" in axioms, n\n    for n in (\"pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary\", \"pathwidth_le_cut\",\n              \"pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree\", \"pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul\"):\n        assert n in sw.CUT_LEMMA_PROVED\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# item 05: `lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/Potential.lean`\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nPOTENTIAL_LEAN = WEIGHTS_LEAN.parent / \"Potential.lean\"\n\n\ndef test_potential_minus_lean_transcription_agrees_with_fminus():\n    \"\"\"The Lean `potentialMinus` (transcribed) equals the Python `fminus` and its per-vertex\n    form on random graphs with isolated vertices; additivity holds on disjoint unions.\"\"\"\n    import random\n    import learning.sandwich as sw\n    from learning.edwards_mcdermid import fminus, support\n    rng = random.Random(505)\n    for _ in range(200):\n        n = rng.randint(1, 11)\n        adj = sw._random_graph_with_isolated(rng, n)\n        assert sw.potential_minus_lean(adj) == fminus(adj)\n        assert sw.potential_minus_lean(adj) == sw.vertex_term_sum_lean(adj)\n        # a disjoint union with a second random graph on the complementary vertices\n        s = support(adj)\n        rest = [v for v in range(n) if not (s >> v) & 1]\n        g2 = [0] * n\n        for i, u in enumerate(rest):\n            for v in rest[i + 1:]:\n                if rng.random() < 0.6:\n                    g2[u] |= 1 << v\n                    g2[v] |= 1 << u\n        union = [a | b for a, b in zip(adj, g2)]\n        assert sw.potential_minus_lean(union) == sw.potential_minus_lean(adj) + sw.potential_minus_lean(g2)\n\n\ndef test_potential_proved_names_are_theorems_in_the_lean_file():\n    \"\"\"Every name `learning.sandwich` audits for `Potential.lean` is declared there as a\n    theorem; the file has no `sorry` and no `axiom`; the root module imports it; and\n    `paper1/axiom_check.lean` prints the axioms of every one.\"\"\"\n    import learning.sandwich as sw\n    src = POTENTIAL_LEAN.read_text()\n    declared = set(re.findall(r\"^(?:@\\[simp\\] )?theorem\\s+([^\\s:({\\[]+)\", src, re.M))\n    missing = [n for n in sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED if n.split(\".\")[-1] not in declared]\n    assert not missing, missing\n    assert all(n.startswith(\"DegreeBound.\") for n in sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED)\n    assert set(sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED) <= set(sw.ALL_PROVED)\n    assert len(sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED) == len(declared) == 54\n    code = re.sub(r\"/-.*?-/\", \"\", src, flags=re.S)\n    code = re.sub(r\"--.*\", \"\", code)\n    assert \"sorry\" not in code\n    assert not re.search(r\"^\\s*axiom\\b\", code, re.M)\n    root = (POTENTIAL_LEAN.parents[2] / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    assert \"import MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound.Potential\\n\" in root\n    axioms = (POTENTIAL_LEAN.parents[3] / \"paper1\" / \"axiom_check.lean\").read_text()\n    for n in sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED:\n        assert f\"#print axioms MOSPFormalization.{n}\\n\" in axioms, n\n    for n in (\"degree_isolate\", \"potential_isolate\", \"potential_isolate_le_sub_one\",\n              \"potential_isolate_regular\", \"potentialMinus_le_potential\",\n              \"potentialMinus_eq_sum_compPotential\", \"compPotential_nonneg\",\n              \"potentialMinus_eq_sum_vertexTerm\", \"potentialMinus_le_F\",\n              \"potentialMinus_eq_F_of_connected\", \"potentialMinus_add\",\n              \"potentialMinus_cubic\", \"potentialMinus_ge_five_sixths\"):\n        assert f\"DegreeBound.{n}\" in sw.POTENTIAL_PROVED\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# item 06: `lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/SPReduction.lean` — the reduction system\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSP_REDUCTION_LEAN = WEIGHTS_LEAN.parent / \"SPReduction.lean\"\n\n\ndef _step_kind(adj, v):\n    nb = adj[v]\n    if nb.bit_count() == 1:\n        return \"pendant\"\n    x = (nb & -nb).bit_length() - 1\n    y = (nb ^ (nb & -nb)).bit_length() - 1\n    return \"triangle\" if (adj[x] >> y) & 1 else \"suppress\"\n\n\ndef test_commutation_lemma_in_the_lean_form_on_random_graphs():\n    \"\"\"R3 as `SPStep.isolate_comm` proves it: for a step at `v` and `w ≠ v`, either\n    `H − w = G − w` (then `v` was pendant at `w`) or one step at `v` in `G − w` reaches\n    `H − w`, pendant if `w ∈ N(v)` and of the original kind otherwise; R3X for a random\n    finset `X ∌ v`; R4 along a random maximal reduction with `X ⊆ supp H`; R5 with a\n    graph `K` supported away from `G`; a vertex of degree 1 or 2 admits a step (the\n    witness of `exists_spStep_of_ndeg`).\"\"\"\n    import random\n    from learning.edwards_mcdermid import (bits, isolate, isolate_set, sp_step, step_vertices,\n                                          support)\n    rng = random.Random(606)\n    triples = 0\n    for _ in range(300):\n        n = rng.randint(2, 11)\n        p = rng.choice([0.15, 0.3, 0.5])\n        adj = [0] * n\n        for a in range(n):\n            for b in range(a + 1, n):\n                if rng.random() < p:\n                    adj[a] |= 1 << b\n                    adj[b] |= 1 << a\n        for v in step_vertices(adj):\n            H = sp_step(adj, v)\n            kind = _step_kind(adj, v)\n            assert H[v] == 0 and sum(h.bit_count() for h in H) < sum(a.bit_count() for a in adj)\n            assert all(H[u].bit_count() <= adj[u].bit_count() for u in range(n))\n            for w in range(n):\n                if w == v:\n                    continue\n                triples += 1\n                Gw, Hw = isolate(adj, w), isolate(H, w)\n                if Hw == Gw:\n                    assert kind == \"pendant\" and (adj[v] >> w) & 1\n                    continue\n                assert 1 <= Gw[v].bit_count() <= 2 and sp_step(Gw, v) == Hw\n                assert _step_kind(Gw, v) == (\"pendant\" if (adj[v] >> w) & 1 else kind)\n            X = sum(1 << u for u in range(n) if u != v and rng.random() < 0.4)\n            GX, HX = isolate_set(adj, X), isolate_set(H, X)\n            assert HX == GX or (1 <= GX[v].bit_count() <= 2 and sp_step(GX, v) == HX)\n            s = support(adj)\n            rest = [u for u in range(n) if not (s >> u) & 1]\n            K = [0] * n\n            for i, a in enumerate(rest):\n                for b in rest[i + 1:]:\n                    if rng.random() < 0.6:\n                        K[a] |= 1 << b\n                        K[b] |= 1 << a\n            GK = [a | k for a, k in zip(adj, K)]\n            assert sp_step(GK, v) == [h | k for h, k in zip(H, K)]\n        # R4 along a random maximal reduction\n        seq, cur = [], list(adj)\n        while step_vertices(cur):\n            v = rng.choice(step_vertices(cur))\n            seq.append(v)\n            cur = sp_step(cur, v)\n        assert all(cur[v] == 0 for v in seq)\n        X = sum(1 << u for u in bits(support(cur)) if rng.random() < 0.5)\n        g_cur = isolate_set(adj, X)\n        for v in seq:\n            assert not (X >> v) & 1\n            if 1 <= g_cur[v].bit_count() <= 2:\n                g_cur = sp_step(g_cur, v)\n        assert g_cur == isolate_set(cur, X)\n    assert triples > 1000\n\n\ndef test_item06_brute_force_log_has_no_violation():\n    \"\"\"The exhaustive check to 9 vertices (`06_reduction/check_r3.py`) was run and found\n    nothing; its R3 counts are item 02's.\"\"\"\n    import json\n    p = SP_REDUCTION_LEAN.parents[3] / \"reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/06_reduction/summary.json\"\n    if not p.exists():\n        pytest.skip(\"brute-force summary not present\")\n    s = json.loads(p.read_text())\n    assert s[\"violations\"] == 0\n    assert s[\"total\"][\"R3\"] == 3115987 and s[\"total\"][\"R3_zero\"] == 95300\n    assert s[\"total\"][\"R1\"] == 393156\n\n\ndef test_sp_reduction_proved_names_are_theorems_in_the_lean_file():\n    \"\"\"Every name `learning.sandwich` audits for `SPReduction.lean` is declared there as a\n    theorem (namespaces resolved); the file has no `sorry` and no `axiom`; the root module\n    imports it; `paper1/axiom_check.lean` prints the axioms of every one; the statements\n    the later items need are present.\"\"\"\n    import learning.sandwich as sw\n    src = SP_REDUCTION_LEAN.read_text()\n    code = re.sub(r\"/-.*?-/\", \"\", src, flags=re.S)\n    ns, declared = [], set()\n----SW\nSP_REDUCTION_PROVED = (\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_eq_degree\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_eq_zero_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_pos_of_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_le_of_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_bot\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_eq_one_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_eq_two_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_sup\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_edge_left\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_edge_right\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_edge_of_ne\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_eq_self_of_forall_not_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_eq_self_of_ndeg_eq_zero\",\n    \"DegreeBound.neighborSet_isolate\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_isolate_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_isolate_self\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_empty\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_singleton\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_insert\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolateSet_comm_isolate\",\n    \"DegreeBound.ndeg_isolateSet_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_eq_self\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_sup_restrict_compl\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isolate_restrict\",\n    \"DegreeBound.restrict_adj_imp_not_adj_compl\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isSPReduced_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isSPReduced_bot\",\n    \"DegreeBound.isBasic_bot\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.refl\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.trans\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.single\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.head\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.tail\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.not_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_self\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.exists_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_pos\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_eq\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_isolate_sup_edge_left\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_isolate_sup_edge_of_ne\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.ndeg_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.degSum_lt\",\n    \"DegreeBound.not_isSPReduced_iff\",\n    \"DegreeBound.exists_spStep_of_ndeg\",\n    \"DegreeBound.exists_spStep_of_not_isSPReduced\",\n    \"DegreeBound.IsSPReduced.not_spStep\",\n    \"DegreeBound.exists_reduced_reduct\",\n    \"DegreeBound.IsSPReduced.eq_of_spReduces\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.ndeg_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.degree_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.ndeg_eq_zero\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.not_adj_of_not_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.supp_subset\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.potential_le\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.potential_sub_ge_of_isolated\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.isolate_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.isolateSet_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPStep.sup_of_disjoint\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.not_spStep_of_adj\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.isolateSet_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.isolate_comm\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.isolate_comm_of_isolated\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.sup_of_disjoint\",\n    \"DegreeBound.SPReduces.sup_of_disjoint_supp\",\n)\n#: Every proved name the axiom check asks for.\nALL_PROVED = (PROVED + FOREST_COVER_PROVED + PENDANT_PROVED + SEPARATOR_PROVED + DEGREE_BOUND_PROVED\n              + CUT_LEMMA_PROVED + POTENTIAL_PROVED + SP_REDUCTION_PROVED)\n#: Statements committed with `sorry`: none since 2026-10-31.\nSTATED: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# The Lean definitions, transcribed\n----GATE\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Regression gate for loop0012 (the Edwards–McDermid degree-sequence bound).\n\nPasses only if all five hold:\n1. `lake build` in lean/ succeeds;\n2. every `.lean` file under lean/MOSPFormalization/ (top level, Complex/ and\n   Search/) is imported by lean/MOSPFormalization.lean, so the build really\n   checks it;\n3. the number of `sorry` in Lean *code* (comments and docstrings stripped) is\n   at most the baseline (0: the development has none since Appendix E) plus\n   the entries in allowed_sorries.txt, and no `axiom` declaration exists;\n4. `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes, and so does `pytest` in\n   pathwidth_solver/;\n5. the paper builds with no undefined references (`make -C paper1/latex check`).\n\n    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0012/gate.py\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[1]\nLEAN = REPO / \"lean\"\nBASELINE_SORRIES = 0\nALLOWED = HERE / \"allowed_sorries.txt\"\nPAPER = REPO / \"paper1\" / \"latex\"\n\n\ndef strip_comments(src: str) -> str:\n    out, i, depth = [], 0, 0\n    while i < len(src):\n        if src.startswith(\"/-\", i):\n            depth += 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth and src.startswith(\"-/\", i):\n            depth -= 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth:\n            i += 1; continue\n        if src.startswith(\"--\", i):\n            j = src.find(\"\\n\", i); i = len(src) if j < 0 else j; continue\n        if src[i] == '\"':\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(src) and src[j] != '\"':\n                j += 2 if src[j] == \"\\\\\" else 1\n            i = j + 1; continue\n        out.append(src[i]); i += 1\n    return \"\".join(out)\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    ok = True\n    b = subprocess.run([\"lake\", \"build\"], cwd=LEAN, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    tail = \"\\n\".join((b.stdout + b.stderr).splitlines()[-25:])\n    if b.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: lake build\\n\" + tail); return 1\n    print(\"lake build: ok\")\n\n    root = (LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        mod = \"MOSPFormalization.\" + \".\".join(f.relative_to(LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").with_suffix(\"\").parts)\n        if not re.search(rf\"^import {re.escape(mod)}\\s*$\", root, re.M):\n            print(f\"GATE FAIL: {mod} is not imported by MOSPFormalization.lean\"); ok = False\n\n    sorries, axioms = [], []\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        code = strip_comments(f.read_text())\n        for n, line in enumerate(code.splitlines(), 1):\n            if re.search(r\"\\bsorry\\b\", line):\n                sorries.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n            if re.match(r\"\\s*(private\\s+)?axiom\\b\", line):\n                axioms.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n    allowed = [l for l in ALLOWED.read_text().splitlines() if l.strip() and not l.startswith(\"#\")] if ALLOWED.exists() else []\n    limit = BASELINE_SORRIES + len(allowed)\n    print(f\"sorry in code: {len(sorries)} (limit {limit}): {sorries}\")\n    if len(sorries) > limit:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: more sorry than the baseline plus allowed_sorries.txt\"); ok = False\n    if axioms:\n----MINOR\n154:def isolate (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : SimpleGraph V where\n155-  Adj x y := G.Adj x y ∧ x ≠ v ∧ y ≠ v\n156-  symm := ⟨fun _ _ ⟨h, hx, hy⟩ => ⟨h.symm, hy, hx⟩⟩\n157-  loopless := ⟨fun x h => G.loopless.irrefl x h.1⟩\n158-\n159-theorem isolate_le (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : isolate G v ≤ G := fun _ _ h => h.1\n160-\n----REPORT6\n## 6. Lean (iii): the series-parallel reduction system, basic graphs, degree monotonicity, and the commutation of deletion with reduction (item 06, 2026-11-02)\n\n**Deliverable.** `lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/SPReduction.lean`\n(namespace `MOSPFormalization.DegreeBound`, imports `Potential`): the four\noperations of Edwards & McDermid (2015, p. 8) as a step relation on\n`SimpleGraph V` with removed vertices isolated, its reflexive–transitive\nclosure, \"reduced\", \"basic\", and **69 theorems, no `sorry`, no `axiom`**,\nevery one `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. R1–R5 of §2.2 are all\nproved; R6 (optional, not needed by the assembly) is not. No confluence fact\nis stated or used: the paper's Lemma 3.1 (which cites Kneis et al. 2009) is\nreplaced by the local commutation lemma R3 and its lifts R3X / R4, as plan\n§0.5 said. Imported by `lean/MOSPFormalization.lean`; `lake build` passes\n(`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/06_reduction/lake_build.log`).\n\n**Regenerate.** `cd lean && lake build`; `make -C paper1/latex axioms`;\n`nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/06_reduction/check_r3.py --max-n 9 --workers 8`\n(3 s on 8 workers at load 0.3; `check_r3.log`, `summary.json`).\n\n**Size range.** The Lean statements hold on every finite graph (kernel-checked).\nThe brute-force check is every graph on 1–9 vertices from `nauty-geng`\n(288,266), exhaustive for R1, R2, R3, EX, and random for the finset and\nsequence forms (R3X, R4, R5); nothing beyond 9 vertices was checked.\n\n### 6.1 Checked before stated (`06_reduction/check_r3.py`, `check_r3.log`, `summary.json`)\n\nItem 02 had R1–R5 on every graph to 9 (§2.3); the item asked for R3's stage\nto be re-run here. It was re-run **in the form the Lean proof produces**, which\nis stronger than item 02's: R3 records not only that `H − w = G − w` or that\none step at `v` in `G − w` reaches `H − w`, but *which* case and *which\nconstructor* — zero steps exactly when `v` is pendant at `w`; one step of the\noriginal kind when `w ∉ N(v)`, a pendant deletion when `w ∈ N(v)`. The\nstatements beyond §2.6 (R3X, the hypothesis form of R4, R5 in the `⊔` form,\nthe step-existence lemma) were checked for the first time.\n\n| statement | checked on | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| EX: a vertex of degree 1 or 2 admits a step (`exists_spStep_of_ndeg`) | 2,579,255 (graph, vertex) | 0 failures |\n| R1: `degSum H < degSum G` and `ndeg H v = 0 < ndeg G v` | 393,156 steps | 0 |\n| R2: no degree rises; `f H ≤ f G`; an isolated vertex costs `≥ g(deg)` | 393,156 steps, every vertex | 0 |\n| R3 with the constructor kind | 3,115,987 (graph, step, `w`): **95,300 zero-step, all pendant-at-`w`; 3,020,687 one-step, all of the predicted kind** | 0 |\n| R3X: `v ∉ X` random (3 per step) | 1,179,468 (257,776 zero, 921,692 one) | 0 |\n| R4: replay along a random maximal reduction with random `X ⊆ supp H` | 864,798 (graph, `X`) over 288,266 sequences; every acted vertex isolated in `H` | 0 |\n| R5: `SPStep (G ⊔ K) v (H ⊔ K)`, same kind, `K` random on `V ∖ supp G` | 25,566 | 0 |\n\nThe R3 totals (3,115,987 / 95,300 / 3,020,687) are item 02's to the triple.\n**Kill checks: none fired.**\n\n### 6.2 Definitions\n\n- `ndeg G v := (G.neighborSet v).ncard` — the degree with no decidability\n  instance; `ndeg_eq_degree` pins it to `G.degree v` under any\n  `DecidableRel G.Adj`; `degSum G := ∑ v, ndeg G v`.\n- `isolateSet G X` (`G − X`, `X : Finset V`): `Adj a b := G.Adj a b ∧ a ∉ X ∧ b ∉ X`;\n  `restrict G S` (`G|S`, `S : Set V`): `Adj a b := G.Adj a b ∧ a ∈ S ∧ b ∈ S`.\n- `inductive SPStep (G : SimpleGraph V) (v : V) : SimpleGraph V → Prop` with\n  `pendant (hx : G.Adj v x) (hall : ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x) : SPStep G v (isolate G v)`\n  (operation 2), `suppress (hx) (hy) (hxy : x ≠ y) (hall : ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x ∨ z = y) (hnadj : ¬ G.Adj x y) : SPStep G v (isolate G v ⊔ edge x y)`\n  (operation 3), `triangle (…) (hadj : G.Adj x y) : SPStep G v (isolate G v)`\n  (operation 4). Operation 1 is the identity on `SimpleGraph V` (§2.1 (1)).\n- `SPReduces G H := Relation.ReflTransGen (fun G H => ∃ v, SPStep G v H) G H`;\n  `IsSPReduced G := ∀ v, ndeg G v = 0 ∨ 3 ≤ ndeg G v`;\n  `IsBasic G := ∀ C : G.ConnectedComponent, (∃ v ∈ C.supp, 0 < ndeg G v) → (∀ v ∈ C.supp, ndeg G v = 3) ∨ ∃ v ∈ C.supp, SPReduces (isolate (restrict G C.supp) v) ⊥`.\n\n### 6.3 The statements and their proofs\n\nThe instance-free degree (7): `ndeg_eq_degree`, `ndeg_eq_zero_iff`\n(`↔ ∀ z, ¬ G.Adj v z`), `ndeg_pos_of_adj`, `ndeg_le_of_le`, `ndeg_bot`,\n`ndeg_eq_one_iff` (`↔ ∃ x, G.Adj v x ∧ ∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x`, from\n....\n### 6.4 Choices beyond §2.6\n\n1. **The step carries its vertex and states the neighbourhood by adjacency\n   facts, not degrees.** `SPStep G v H` (the item's \"if R3's acted-on vertex\n   needs to be recorded, make `SPStep` carry it from the start\": it does —\n   R3 is stated at `v`, and R4's induction needs `v ∉ X`). The constructors\n   take `G.Adj v x` and `∀ z, G.Adj v z → z = x` (or `z = x ∨ z = y` with\n   `x ≠ y`) rather than `G.degree v = 1` / `2`, so the relation needs no\n   decidability instance and the case analysis of R3 is propositional\n   (`tauto` closes every graph identity).\n2. **An instance-free degree.** `exists_reduced_reduct`'s `H` and the\n   intermediate graphs of every `ReflTransGen` induction carry no\n   `DecidableRel`; `ndeg` (`Set.ncard`) makes `IsSPReduced`, `IsBasic`, R1 and\n   R2 instance-free, and `ndeg_eq_degree` (any instance) converts at the\n   boundary. No `Subsingleton.elim` on instances was needed anywhere.\n3. **R1 on the degree sum, not the edge count.** §2.6 listed\n   `SPStep.edgeFinset_card_lt`; the degree sum drops by 2 (pendant,\n   suppression) or 4 (triangle), and its strict decrease is R2 plus the\n   strict drop at `v` — one `Finset.sum_lt_sum` instead of an edge-set case\n   analysis. `degSum` is the measure of the strong induction.\n4. **`isolateSet` is defined directly**, not as the fold of `isolate` (plan\n   §0.5); `isolateSet_insert` is the fold's step and `isolateSet_singleton`\n   the base, so the fold is recoverable as a theorem.\n5. **R4's hypothesis is `∀ w ∈ X, ∃ z, H.Adj w z`** (`X ⊆ supp H`), the\n   parenthetical option of §2.6, and the proof is by head induction on the\n   sequence rather than by induction on `X` first: an acted vertex ends\n   isolated and stays isolated, so `X ⊆ supp H` keeps `X` clear of every step,\n   and R3X (proved by `Finset` induction from R3) does one step at a time. A\n   Finset-first induction would need the hypothesis for `X ∖ {w}` on\n   `H − w`, where `w`'s removal can isolate other vertices of `X` — the form\n   §2.6 wrote does not go through directly; this one does, and it is the\n   form item 08 uses (`X* ⊆ supp G*`).\n6. **R5's disjointness is instance-free**, `∀ a b, K.Adj a b → ∀ z, ¬ G.Adj a z`,\n   with the `supp` form as a corollary; along a sequence it is preserved\n   because supports shrink.\n7. **`restrict` lives here** (item 05 left it to item 08), with\n   `restrict_sup_restrict_compl`, `isolate_restrict` and `restrict_eq_self`\n   for item 08's disconnected case and for item 07's `nonbasic_reduct_ne_bot`\n   (where the support is one component and `restrict G C.supp = G`).\n8. **R6 is not proved.** It is optional, not what A1 needs, and the budget\n   went to R3–R5.\n\n### 6.5 Axiom lines, tests, regenerate\n\n- 69 new `#print axioms` lines in `paper1/axiom_check.lean`\n  (`06_reduction/axiom_check.log`); `make -C paper1/latex axioms`: **494\n  theorems checked, 0 failures**, every line `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.\n  `SP_REDUCTION_PROVED` (69 names) is folded into `learning.sandwich.ALL_PROVED`.\n- Tests: 3 new in `tests/test_edwards_mcdermid.py` (41 in all): R3 in the\n  Lean form (constructor kinds), R3X, R4 along random maximal reductions, R5\n  and EX on 300 random graphs at 2–11 vertices; the brute-force summary's\n  counts and zero violations; the 69 names declared (namespaces resolved) /\n  imported / audited, no `sorry`, no `axiom`, the constructors and\n  definitions present.\n- No new sandwich stage: nothing here is numerical. The item's\n  `potential_le` and `potential_sub_ge_of_isolated` are the Lean forms of the\n  R2 rows item 02 checked (`R2f`, `R2iso`).\n\n### 6.6 Kill verdict, and what this does not claim\n\n**Kill verdict: none** (the item has no kill criterion); R3 and R4 fitted, so\nitem 08 states Theorem 3.2 with `SPReduces (G − X) B` as the plan wrote it,\nnot with the paper's `r(G − X) = B` and a `ReductionConfluence` Prop.\n\n**What items 07–09 get.** `SPStep`, `SPReduces`, `IsSPReduced`, `IsBasic`,\n`ndeg`, `isolateSet`, `restrict`; `exists_reduced_reduct` (the `G*` of the\nstep); `SPReduces.ndeg_le` / `degree_le` / `potential_le` /\n`potential_sub_ge_of_isolated` (the hinge `j₄ ≥ g'(d)` of item 07: a vertex\nof degree `d ≥ 3` in `G − w` either survives into `G*` with degree `≤ d`, so\n`g'(δ(G*)) ≥ g'(d)` by W3, or is isolated, so `f(G − w) − f(G*) ≥ g(d) ≥ g'(d)`);\n`IsSPReduced.eq_of_spReduces` and `isSPReduced_iff`; R4\n`SPReduces.isolateSet_comm` with `X* ⊆ supp G*` (item 08's\n`SPReduces (G − w − X*) (G* − X*)`); R5 `SPReduces.sup_of_disjoint` with\n`restrict_sup_restrict_compl` and `potentialMinus_add` (item 08's\ndisconnected case); `IsBasic`'s second clause is existential over reduction\nsequences, so `nonbasic_reduct_ne_bot` (item 07) needs no confluence.\n\n**Does not claim.** Uniqueness of the reduct (measured to 9 in item 02, not\nneeded, not proved); that `SPReduces G ⊥` characterises series-parallel\ngraphs (the paper's \"it follows from the definition\" is not formalised and\n\"series-parallel\" does not appear in Lean); R6; anything about pathwidth\n(item 09) or about the hypotheses (H1), (H3); that the brute-force counts are\nevidence beyond 9 vertices (the Lean theorems are the evidence for every\nfinite graph). The constructor-kind refinement of R3 is a property of *this*\nproof's case analysis, recorded so a reader can match the check to the\nproof, not a claim that the kind is forced.\n/usr/bin/nauty-geng\n01_verify\n02_lemmas\n03_weights\n04_cut\n05_potential\n06_reduction\nSHA256\nem2015.pdf\nem2015.txt","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01At2H5KJqQZHHzMBt5SCWbB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
