ree, then","+the smallest lowest-neighbour degree), with `G' = G − w` and `G*` its canonical reduct","+plus `R` random reducts, record which case of the Lean proof fires and check the","+inequalities the proof combines in that case, in exact rationals:","+","+  D4   Δ = deg w ≥ 4 (`four_le_degree_of_not_isBasic`); `G*` non-empty (`nonbasic_reduct_ne_bot`)","+  SJ   1 + f(G') = f(G) + (Δ−1) g'(Δ) + g'(Δ−1) − S, S = Σ_{v∈N(w)} g'(deg v)","+       (`one_add_potential_isolate`), and the j₁, j₂, j₃ form for a random ordered","+       pair of neighbours (`j_identity`, no sorting)","+  S0   j₄ ≥ g'(d) for every v with deg_{G'}(v) = d ≥ 3 (`j4_ge`), and j₄ ≥ 0","+  SL   S ≥ g'(deg v₀) + (Δ−1) g'(Δ) for every neighbour v₀ (`sum_g'_neighbors_ge`)","+  R    no neighbour of `w` below Δ ⇒ every support vertex has degree Δ","+       (`degree_eq_of_reachable`), δ = Δ, S = Δ g'(Δ), j₄ ≥ g'(Δ−1)","+  A    some v with 3 ≤ deg_{G'}(v) ≤ δ(G) ⇒ j₄ ≥ g'(δ(G))","+  B    otherwise δ(G) = 3 and the minimum-degree vertex is adjacent to `w`;","+  B1     a neighbour of degree ≥ 4 ⇒ j₄ ≥ g'(Δ−1);","+  B2     all neighbours of degree 3 ⇒ S = Δ g'(3), a support vertex `u` of `G*` is not","+         adjacent to `w`, deg_{G'}(u) = deg_G(u) ≥ 3, j₄ ≥ g'(Δ)","+  S1   1 + F(G*) ≤ F(G) and 1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G) (the conclusion)","+","+Usage: nice -n 19 python3 check.py --max-n 9 --workers 8","+\"\"\"","+from __future__ import annotations","+","+import argparse","+import collections","+import json","+import os","+import random","+import subprocess","+import sys","+import time","+from fractions import Fraction","+from multiprocessing import Pool","+","+HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))","+sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath(os.path.join(HERE, \"..\", \"..\", \"..\", \"..\")))","+","+from learning.edwards_mcdermid import (  # noqa: E402","+    F_global, bits, components, degrees, f_potential, fminus, g, g_prime, global_min_degree,","+    is_basic, is_reduced, isolate, paper_choice, parse_g6, reduce, reduce_random,","+)","+","+RANDOM_REDUCTS = 3","+","+","+def one(args: tuple[int, str]) -> dict:","+    idx, line = args","+    n, adj = parse_g6(line)","+    rng = random.Random(idx * 7_919 + n)","+    cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()","+    viol: list[str] = []","+","+    def bad(stmt: str, detail: str) -> None:","+        viol.append(f\"{stmt}\\t{line.strip()}\\t{detail}\")","+","+    deg = degrees(adj)","+    supp = [v for v in range(n) if adj[v]]","+    assert len(components(adj)) == 1 and is_reduced(adj) and all(deg[v] >= 3 for v in supp)","+    cnt[\"graphs\"] += 1","+    if is_basic(adj):","+        cnt[\"basic\"] += 1","+        return {\"cnt\": cnt, \"viol\": viol}","+    cnt[\"nonbasic\"] += 1","+    maxs, chosen, D = paper_choice(adj)","+    if D < 4:","+        bad(\"D4\", f\"Δ={D}\")","+    delta = global_min_degree(adj)","+    fG = f_potential(adj)","+    FG = F_global(adj)","+    fmG = fminus(adj)","+    for w in chosen:","+        cnt[\"pairs\"] += 1","+        Gp = isolate(adj, w)","+        dp = degrees(Gp)","+        nbrs = list(bits(adj[w]))","+        S = sum((g_prime(deg[v]) for v in nbrs), Fraction(0))","+        fGp = f_potential(Gp)","+        # SJ, unsorted","+        if 1 + fGp != fG + (D - 1) * g_prime(D) + g_prime(D - 1) - S:","+            bad(\"SJ\", f\"w={w}\")","+        cnt[\"SJ\"] += 1","+        # j-identity for a random ordered pair of distinct neighbours (no sorting)","+        v1, v2 = rng.sample(nbrs, 2)","+        rest = [v for v in nbrs if v not in (v1, v2)]","+        j1 = g_prime(deg[v1]) - g_prime(D - 1)","+        j2 = g_prime(deg[v2]) - g_prime(D)","+        j3 = sum((g_prime(deg[v]) - g_prime(D) for v in rest), Fraction(0))","+        if 1 + fGp != fG - j1 - j2 - j3:","+            bad(\"SJpair\", f\"w={w} v1={v1} v2={v2}\")","+        cnt[\"SJpair\"] += 1","+        # SL for every neighbour","+        for v0 in nbrs:","+            cnt[\"SL\"] += 1","+            if not S >= g_prime(deg[v0]) +