ces (as instance fields, registered with `attribute [instance]`),","+  `reduced`, `conn` (`∀ u ∈ supp G, ∀ v ∈ supp G, G.Reachable u v`),","+  `notBasic`, `maxDeg`, `tieBreak`, `reduces : SPReduces (isolate G w) Gs`,","+  `reducedGs`. Neither `Δ ≥ 4` nor `Gs ≠ ⊥` is a field: both are derived.","+","+### 7.3 The statements and their proofs, and the case table","+","+**Non-basic graphs (5).** `supp_nonempty_of_not_isBasic` (`⊥` is basic);","+`three_le_globalMinDeg` (reduced, non-empty support ⇒ `δ ≥ 3`);","+`four_le_degree_of_not_isBasic` — if the maximum degree were `≤ 3`, every","+non-trivial component would be cubic (its vertices are reachable from a","+positive-degree vertex, so lie in the support, so have degree `3`), and `G`","+basic; `isBasic_of_spReduces_bot` — on a connected support, `SPReduces (G − w) ⊥`","+makes the one component of the second kind, witnessed by `w` (the","+`restrict G C.supp = G` identity by `restrict_eq_self`); hence","+`nonbasic_reduct_ne_bot : SPReduces (isolate G w) Gs → Gs ≠ ⊥` for **every**","+reduct, from the definition of `IsBasic` alone (§2.1 (6)): no confluence.","+`exists_pos_degree_of_ne_bot` turns `≠ ⊥` into a vertex of positive degree.","+","+**The identity (2).** `one_add_potential_isolate` (SJ): P1 and W4 by","+`linarith`. `j_identity`: the paper's (4) for *any* two distinct","+neighbours `v₁ ≠ v₂` — `add_sum_erase` twice, `sum_sub_distrib`, the cast","+`|N(w) ∖ {v₁, v₂}| = Δ − 2`, `ring`. The paper sorts the neighbours by","+degree; the identity holds for every labelling, and the sorted `v₁` is","+used only through the *bounds* below, never through the identity.","+","+**The hinge and the sums (4).** `j4_ge` (S0): `g' d ≤ f(G') − f(G*) + g'(δ(G*))`","+whenever `deg_{G'} v = d`, by cases on `Gs.degree v = 0` — isolated:","+`potential_sub_ge_of_isolated` and `g'_le_g`; surviving: `v ∈ supp Gs`,","+`δ(G*) ≤ deg_{G*} v ≤ d` (R2), `3 ≤ δ(G*)` (reduced), W3, and","+`potential_le`. The paper's `d ≥ 3` is not needed and not taken (for","+`d ≤ 2` the statement is `0 ≤ j₄`). `j4_nonneg`. `sum_g'_neighbors_ge`:","+every neighbour's term is `≥ g'(Δ)` (W3), one term kept exact — the inside","+of P2's proof, stated so that each branch can choose its `v₀`.","+`sum_g'_neighbors_eq`: all neighbours of one degree `d` ⇒ `S = Δ g'(d)`.","+","+**The regular case (1).** `degree_eq_of_reachable`: if no neighbour of","+`w` is below `Δ`, then `minNbrDeg G w = Δ`, so by the tie-break every","+maximum-degree `x` has `minNbrDeg G x ≥ Δ`, i.e. all its neighbours have","+degree `Δ`; this propagates along any walk from `w` (induction on","+`G.Walk x y` with the invariant `deg x = Δ`). This is the paper's \"`d(v₁) < Δ`","+unless `G` is `Δ`-regular\" and **the only place the tie-break is used** —","+exactly where item 02 found S1′ failing (§2.4).","+","+**S1 (2 + 2).** `one_add_F_le`: after `unfold F` and SJ, it suffices that","+`g'(δ) + (Δ − 1) g'(Δ) + g'(Δ − 1) ≤ S + j₄`, and the four branches close it:","+","+| paper (pp. 11–12) | branch of `one_add_F_le` | what it uses | closes by |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| \"If `G` is `Δ`-regular, then `d(v₁) = Δ`, and `G'` will contain a vertex of degree `Δ − 1`, so `j₄ ≥ g'(Δ − 1)`\" | `hreg : ∀ v, G.Adj w v → deg v = Δ` | `degree_eq_of_reachable` (so `δ = Δ`), `sum_g'_neighbors_eq`, `j4_ge` at a neighbour (`deg_{G'} = Δ − 1`) | `linarith` |","+| \"Otherwise `d(v₁) ≤ Δ − 1`, so `j₁ ≥ 0`. If `G'` contains `v` with `δ(G) ≥ d_{G'}(v) ≥ 3`, then `j ≥ j₄ ≥ g'(δ(G))`\" | `¬ hreg`, `hA : ∃ v, 3 ≤ deg_{G'} v ≤ δ` | `sum_g'_neighbors_ge` at the low neighbour `v₀` (`g'(deg v₀) ≥ g'(Δ − 1)`), `j4_ge` at `v`, W3 | `linarith` |","+| \"So suppose not. Then `δ(G) = 3` … every vertex with `d_G(v) = 3` must be a neighbour of `w`\" | `¬ hA`: the minimum-degree vertex `v₁ ≠ w` has `deg_{G'} v₁ ∈ {δ, δ − 1}`, so `δ = 3` and `G.Adj w v₁` | `exists_degree_eq_globalMinDeg`, `degree_isolate_of_adj` / `_of_not_adj`, `omega` | — |","+| \"If `d(v_Δ) > 3`, then `v_Δ` satisfies `Δ − 1 ≥ d_{G'}(v_Δ) ≥ 3`